<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n6664" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caprĕae</span></b> , ārum,
			f., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>an island in the Tyrrhene Sea</i>, <i>near
				Campania</i>, now <i>Capri</i>, <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 6,
				12, § 82</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Verg. A. 7,
				735</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 15, 709</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Sil. 8,
			541</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">celebrated as the dwelling-place of the emperor
					Tiberius,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac. A.
					4, 67</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">6, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 2</span></i>; 6, 10; <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 39</span></i>; <i><span class="en">40</span></i>; <i><span class="en">60</span></i>; 62; 74; <i><span class="en">Juv. 10,
			72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">10, 93</span></i>;
			who was thence, and in derision of his wantonness, called <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Caprinēus</span></b> , <i><span class="en">Suet.
				Tib. 43</span></i>.—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Ca-prĕensis</span></b> , e,
			adj.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">secessus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Suet. Tib. 43</span></i>
			.</div>
